Slot 0117 (FG-loop drawTileFast inline) measured +5 fps on the FG-
tilemap render path by replacing Renderer::drawSurface's entry chain
with a direct call to the INDEX8→INDEX8 hand-rolled _blit_indexed
primitive. This patch extends the same mechanism to the BG-tilemap
cache-fill path (slot 0097 Path B): tile blits into the cache surface
go through SDL_BlitSurface, which has format-dispatch overhead that
_blit_indexed skips.

Mechanism. New methods on the Tileset / Renderer pair:

- Tileset::drawTileFastToSurface(target, x, y, t)
- Renderer::drawTileFastToSurface(src, target, dstx, dsty, srcx, srcy)

Mirror of drawTileFast / Renderer::drawTileFast but with a target-
surface override (rather than the cached window surface). The
Renderer-side method calls `_blit_indexed(target, src_sfc, srcrect,
dstrect, colorkey, has_colorkey)` directly when src and target are
both INDEX8. Defensive fallback: if format precondition fails (rare;
indicates Wave-16 indexed-mode invariant violation), falls back to
SDL_BlitSurface — the fallback path increments the engagement
discriminator `fallback` counter to surface the unexpected mode.

Caller (`map.cpp::_tilemap_render_plain_tiles_into_cache`) reads the
new env-helper `drawtile_fast_bg_active()` once at function entry
(cached static-const-bool; -O3 hoists out of the per-tile loop) and
dispatches each per-tile cache-fill call through
`tileset.drawTileFastToSurface(cache, ...)` when env on or
`tileset.drawTileToSurface(cache, ...)` when env off. Per-tile
counter bumps `calls` unconditionally + `engaged` or `fallback`
depending on dispatch path — flush-instr's wave-35 contract § 5.3
fast-path-engagement discriminator.

Killswitch. `SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DRAWTILE_FAST_BG=0` (strict-"0"
disables; default ON; mirror of patches 0088 / 0093 / 0117 / 0126 /
0128 / 0130 inverse-killswitch convention). Independent of slot
0117's `SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DRAWTILE_FAST` per flush-instr's contract
spec — separate killswitch allows wave-35 A/B PLAY4 to isolate
slot-0132 effect from slot-0117's FG-loop effect. (My initial lean
was to share slot 0117's killswitch since the mechanism is uniform;
flush-instr overrode for A/B-isolation clarity.)

Per-block engagement counters in NXE::Diag (Renderer.cpp storage;
diagnostic_timers.h externs; per-block reset alongside the existing
FLIP_INSTR audit-flush family):

- g_drawtile_fast_bg_calls_count_block — total per-tile cache-fill
  calls (regardless of env state)
- g_drawtile_fast_bg_engaged_count_block — fast-path dispatches
- g_drawtile_fast_bg_fallback_count_block — slot-0097-fallback
  dispatches (env off OR format mismatch)

Equality holds modulo NULL-tileset early-return:
`engaged + fallback ≈ calls` per block.

Emit line in `_maybe_flush_phase_timing_audit` gated on FLIP_INSTR:

  [drawtile-fast-bg n=100 engaged=N fallback=N calls=N]

flush-instr's grep tooling uses engagement rate as the load-bearing
discriminator before attributing fps delta to the patch mechanism.

Predicted savings + architectural caveat. Per flush-instr's wave-35
contract § 5.3: -3 to -8 ms / flip predicted (anchored on slot 0117's
+5 fps measured-precedent for the FG-loop). **Important caveat**:
slot 0117's precedent fired EVERY FRAME (FG-loop dispatch is per-
flip, per-tile, ~100-200 tiles), whereas slot 0132 fires only on
BG-tilemap cache FILLS — which happen on slot 0097 cache MISSES.
In steady-state gameplay the BG cache hit rate is typically ~95-100%,
so cache-fill only runs on map transitions or rare invalidations.
The per-flip amortized savings may be substantially smaller than the
precedent suggests. Wave-35 PLAY3-PLAY4 measurement is the load-
bearing architectural test:

- If delta ∈ [+3, +8 fps]: CPU-bound class translates; absorption-
  by-wall-clock-sink is bucket-dependent. wave-36+ direction =
  more CPU-bound levers in similar code paths.
- If delta ≈ 0 fps: absorption applies universally OR engagement
  frequency was too low; wave-36+ direction = Phase 12 audio attack
  becomes the only remaining viable lever.

Either outcome is informative per `cpu_savings_absorbed_by_wall_-
clock_sink.md` companion memory.

Architectural classification. Pure CPU-bound win (eliminates
SDL_BlitSurface format-dispatch overhead; inline _blit_indexed
memcpy/colorkey loop). Same class as slot 0117 (FG) / slot 0128
(H3 visit-loop). Subject to absorption-by-wall-clock-sink risk.

Smoke. Builds clean at i486 -O3 -funroll-loops -fno-rtti. New strings
in binary: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DRAWTILE_FAST_BG env-var symbol,
[drawtile-fast-bg n=100 ...] emit template, drawTileFastToSurface
symbols (both Renderer + Tileset). Prior slot markers (0128 TILE_-
BOUNDS_SKIP, 0129 snd-shutdown[3.5/6], 0130 BG_SUBREGION_BLIT, 0131
P12_AUDIO_INSTR, 0126 thrashing-detect engaged, 0117 DRAWTILE_FAST)
all retained. Slot 0127 Lever B markers still absent (wave-32
revert intact).

