+// primitive — same code path drawTileFast (slot 0117) uses for the
+// FG-tilemap window write. When DISABLED (env=0), the original
+// `drawTileToSurface` (slot 0097) path runs unchanged: single
+// SDL_BlitSurface per tile with format-dispatch overhead.
+//
+// Polarity: only literal "0" disables (mirror of inverse-killswitch
+// convention). Any other value (unset, empty, "1", garbage) keeps the
+// fast path engaged. Cached lambda + static const bool so the per-
+// call dispatch guard is hoisted by -O3.
+//
+// Predicted savings: -3 to -8 ms / flip (per slot 0117's +5 fps
+// measured-precedent at +5 fps on FG-loop drawTile/drawTileFast swap;
+// flush-instr's wave-35 contract § 5.3). HOWEVER — engagement
+// frequency depends on slot 0097 BG-tilemap cache hit rate. If cache
+// hits ~95% in steady-state gameplay, cache-fill fires only on the
+// remaining ~5% of frames + map transitions, so the per-flip
+// amortized win may be substantially smaller than the precedent
+// suggests. Wave-35 PLAY3 - PLAY4 measurement is the load-bearing
+// test for this architectural class question (see `cpu_savings_-
+// absorbed_by_wall_clock_sink.md` companion memory).
+//
+// Architectural classification. CPU-bound work (eliminate SDL_Blit-
+// Surface dispatch overhead; inline _blit_indexed memcpy loop). Same
+// class as slot 0117 / 0128. Subject to absorption-by-wall-clock-sink
+// risk if the per-flip slack lands inside the audio+engine bucket
+// rather than translating to fps. Wave-35's architectural test
